IMPORT prelude

-- Road Vehicle Standards Act 2018 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the person importing, buying or selling a vehicle
-- meets: what a "road vehicle" is (s 6); who is permitted to import one (s 22); providing a vehicle for the first time in
-- Australia when it is not on the Register of Approved Vehicles (s 24); modifying a vehicle on the RAV before it first
-- reaches a consumer (s 26); a new RAV vehicle on public roads despite State or Territory standards (s 78); and the
-- penalties, including for recalls and infringement notices (ss 16-18, 22, 24, 26-32, 38-40, 56).
--
-- SEAT: the individual who wants to import a vehicle, or to buy or sell one that may not meet the national standards.
-- "Is it a road vehicle? May I import it? May I sell it, or was the seller allowed to sell it to me, if it is not on the
-- RAV? Can I use it on the road? What is the most I can be fined?" Provisions addressed to the Secretary or the Minister are
-- encoded as what they mean for that person: the instruments that put a vehicle in or out of the Act, the approvals.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 3, compilation date 1 January 2025 (includes amendments up to Act No. 35, 2024), as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2018A00163.txt.
--
-- THE RULES ARE NOT DEPOSITED. The Road Vehicle Standards Rules 2018 (s 82) set the entry pathways (s 15), the approvals
-- (ss 19, 23), the further import circumstances (s 22(2)(d)), the further exceptions (s 24(3)(f)), the modifications
-- allowed (s 25) and recall notices (s 37). Each is asked as a fact where a question needs it.
--
-- PENALTIES are in penalty units, as the Act states them. The value of a penalty unit is set by s 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914
-- (indexed), not this Act, and is an input to the one question that turns units into dollars.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Part 1 machinery, ss 12-13 (the standards themselves), ss 14, 19-21 (keeping the registers), s 33-35
-- (executive officers; bodies corporate), Part 3 Divisions 2 and 4 (recall rules, disclosure notices), Parts 4 and 5
-- (enforcement and administration) except the infringement amounts in s 56, ss 76, 79-82.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Road Vehicle Standards Act 2018 -- importing, buying and selling a vehicle`

§§ `s 6 -- is it a road vehicle`

-- s 6(1): "(a) a motor vehicle designed solely or principally for use in transport on public roads; (b) a trailer or other
-- vehicle ... designed to be towed on a public road by a motor vehicle covered by paragraph (a); (c) a vehicle that is within
-- a class determined in an instrument under paragraph (5)(a) and not determined in an instrument under paragraph (6)(b); (d)
-- a vehicle determined in an instrument under paragraph (6)(a); (e) a partly completed or unassembled vehicle that would
-- otherwise be covered". (3): design is judged "only [by] the physical and operational features". (4): not a road vehicle
-- if within a class excluded under (5)(b) and not named under (6)(a), or named under (6)(b). s 5: "motor vehicle" uses
-- "volatile spirit, gas, oil, electricity or any other power (other than human or animal power)" and is not used
-- exclusively on a railway or tramway. The Secretary's instruments are asked as facts.
@export Is my vehicle a "road vehicle" under the Road Vehicle Standards Act?
GIVEN `it is a motor vehicle designed for public roads` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is powered other than by human or animal power (not a rail or tram vehicle), and its physical and operational features show it is designed solely or principally for transport on public roads (or it is a partly built or unassembled vehicle that would be)
      `it is a trailer designed to be towed on public roads` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a trailer, or other wheeled vehicle or equipment, designed to be towed on a public road by such a motor vehicle (or a partly built one)
      `a class instrument says it is a road vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is within a class of vehicles the Secretary has determined, by legislative instrument, to be road vehicles
      `a class instrument says it is not a road vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is within a class of vehicles the Secretary has determined, by legislative instrument, not to be road vehicles
      `an instrument names it as a road vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary has determined, by notifiable instrument, that this particular vehicle is a road vehicle
      `an instrument names it as not a road vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary has determined, by notifiable instrument, that this particular vehicle is not a road vehicle
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my vehicle a road vehicle` IF
    IF `an instrument names it as not a road vehicle`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF `an instrument names it as a road vehicle`
         THEN TRUE
         ELSE IF `a class instrument says it is not a road vehicle`
              THEN FALSE
              ELSE `it is a motor vehicle designed for public roads` OR `it is a trailer designed to be towed on public roads` OR `a class instrument says it is a road vehicle`

§§ `s 22 -- importing a road vehicle`

-- s 22(2): "A person is permitted to import a road vehicle if: (a) at the time of importation" the person holds a road vehicle
-- type approval in force for the vehicle's type; "(b)" is authorised in writing by such a holder; "(c)" holds an import
-- approval in force that specifies the vehicle; "(d) ... a circumstance set out in the rules applies". (1), (3), (4):
-- importing without permission is an offence and a civil penalty, 120 penalty units each.
DECLARE `May I import it` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I hold a road vehicle type approval in force for its type (s 22(2)(a))`
    `yes: the holder of a road vehicle type approval in force for its type has authorised me in writing (s 22(2)(b))`
    `yes: I hold an import approval in force that specifies this vehicle (s 22(2)(c))`
    `yes: a circumstance the rules set out applies (s 22(2)(d))`
    `no: importing it would contravene s 22(1), an offence and a civil penalty of up to 120 penalty units`
    `the Act does not regulate importing it: it is not a road vehicle (s 6)`

@export Am I permitted to import this vehicle into Australia?
GIVEN `it is a road vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a road vehicle under s 6 (a motor vehicle designed for public roads, a trailer for them, or one the Secretary's instruments bring in)
      `I hold a type approval for its type` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when it is imported, you hold a road vehicle type approval that is in force and applies to the vehicle's type
      `a type approval holder has authorised me in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when it is imported, the holder of a road vehicle type approval in force for its type has authorised you in writing to import it
      `I hold an import approval for this vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when it is imported, you hold an import approval (for example a concessional RAV entry or non-RAV entry import approval) that is in force and specifies this vehicle
      `a circumstance in the rules applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when it is imported, a circumstance set out in the Road Vehicle Standards Rules for importing without an approval applies
GIVETH A `May I import it`
`May I import this vehicle` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a road vehicle`)
    THEN `the Act does not regulate importing it: it is not a road vehicle (s 6)`
    ELSE IF `I hold a type approval for its type`
         THEN `yes: I hold a road vehicle type approval in force for its type (s 22(2)(a))`
         ELSE IF `a type approval holder has authorised me in writing`
              THEN `yes: the holder of a road vehicle type approval in force for its type has authorised me in writing (s 22(2)(b))`
              ELSE IF `I hold an import approval for this vehicle`
                   THEN `yes: I hold an import approval in force that specifies this vehicle (s 22(2)(c))`
                   ELSE IF `a circumstance in the rules applies`
                        THEN `yes: a circumstance the rules set out applies (s 22(2)(d))`
                        ELSE `no: importing it would contravene s 22(1), an offence and a civil penalty of up to 120 penalty units`

§§ `s 24 -- providing a vehicle not on the Register of Approved Vehicles`

-- s 24(1): a person contravenes it if "(a) the person provides a road vehicle to another person in Australia; and (b) the
-- vehicle is provided for the first time in Australia; and (c) the vehicle is not on the RAV". s 5(2): "provide" includes
-- sale, exchange, gift, lease, loan, hire or hire-purchase, and giving access. (2)-(3): providing it "(a) to have work done
-- on it; or (b) to protect it; or (c) to store it; or (d) if the vehicle has been imported--to transport it to the importer;
-- or (e) if the vehicle is to be exported--to transport it to the exporter; or (f) in a circumstance set out in the rules"
-- is not a contravention and does not count as the first provision. (4): nor is providing it "(a)" as the holder of a non-RAV
-- entry import approval for it, or "(b)" an Australian-made vehicle where the person "makes it clear to the recipient" that
-- it is not for use on a public road, or only in exceptional circumstances. (5), (6): 120 penalty units.
DECLARE `Why I am providing it` IS ONE OF
    `to sell, give, lend, lease or hire it, or give access to it`
    `to have work done on it`
    `to protect it`
    `to store it`
    `to transport it to the importer, after it was imported`
    `to transport it to the exporter, before it is exported`
    `in a circumstance the rules set out`

DECLARE `May I provide it` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is on the RAV, so s 24 does not stop it`
    `yes: it has already been provided in Australia before, so this is not its first provision (s 24(1)(b))`
    `yes: providing it to have work done, to protect, store or transport it, or in a circumstance in the rules, is not caught (s 24(3))`
    `yes: I hold a non-RAV entry import approval that relates to it (s 24(4)(a))`
    `yes: it is made in Australia and I make it clear it is not for use on a public road, or only in exceptional circumstances (s 24(4)(b))`
    `no: providing it would contravene s 24(1), an offence and a civil penalty of up to 120 penalty units`
    `the Act does not regulate it: it is not a road vehicle (s 6)`

@export May I sell, give or lend this vehicle to someone in Australia if it is not on the Register of Approved Vehicles? (Or: was the seller allowed to provide it to me?)
GIVEN `it is a road vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a road vehicle under s 6
      `it is on the Register of Approved Vehicles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is entered on the Register of Approved Vehicles (RAV)
      `it has been provided to someone in Australia before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has already been sold, given, lent, leased or hired to someone in Australia (not counting handing it over for work, protection, storage or transport)
      `why I am providing it` IS A `Why I am providing it` @desc Why the vehicle is being handed over
      `I hold a non-RAV entry import approval for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person providing it holds a non-RAV entry import approval that relates to the vehicle
      `it is made in Australia and I say it is not for road use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was manufactured in Australia and the person providing it makes clear to the recipient that it is not for use on a public road, or only in exceptional circumstances
GIVETH A `May I provide it`
`May I provide this vehicle` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a road vehicle`)
    THEN `the Act does not regulate it: it is not a road vehicle (s 6)`
    ELSE IF `it is on the Register of Approved Vehicles`
         THEN `yes: it is on the RAV, so s 24 does not stop it`
         ELSE IF `it has been provided to someone in Australia before`
              THEN `yes: it has already been provided in Australia before, so this is not its first provision (s 24(1)(b))`
              ELSE IF `why I am providing it` EQUALS `to sell, give, lend, lease or hire it, or give access to it`
                   THEN IF `I hold a non-RAV entry import approval for it`
                        THEN `yes: I hold a non-RAV entry import approval that relates to it (s 24(4)(a))`
                        ELSE IF `it is made in Australia and I say it is not for road use`
                             THEN `yes: it is made in Australia and I make it clear it is not for use on a public road, or only in exceptional circumstances (s 24(4)(b))`
                             ELSE `no: providing it would contravene s 24(1), an offence and a civil penalty of up to 120 penalty units`
                   ELSE `yes: providing it to have work done, to protect, store or transport it, or in a circumstance in the rules, is not caught (s 24(3))`

§§ `s 26 -- modifying a vehicle on the RAV`

-- s 26(1): a person contravenes it if a road vehicle is on the RAV, the person modifies it, "(c) the modification occurs
-- before the vehicle is provided to a consumer for the first time in Australia", "(d) the modification causes the road
-- vehicle to not satisfy the requirements of the entry pathway that applied at the time the vehicle was entered on the RAV;
-- and (e) the modification is not otherwise allowed by the rules". (2): the same for handing it over to be modified.
-- (4), (5): 120 penalty units. Modifications after the vehicle first reaches a consumer are left to State and Territory law
-- (s 78(4)).
DECLARE `May I modify it` IS ONE OF
    `the Act does not restrict it: s 26 applies only before the vehicle is first provided to a consumer in Australia; State or Territory law governs later modifications and use`
    `yes: the modification does not take it outside the entry pathway it was entered on the RAV under (s 26(1)(d))`
    `yes: the rules allow the modification (s 26(1)(e))`
    `no: the modification would contravene s 26, an offence and a civil penalty of up to 120 penalty units`
    `s 26 does not apply: the vehicle is not on the RAV`

@export May I modify this vehicle on the Register of Approved Vehicles (or have it modified)?
GIVEN `it is on the Register of Approved Vehicles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a road vehicle entered on the Register of Approved Vehicles
      `it has already been provided to a consumer in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has already been sold, leased or otherwise provided to a consumer in Australia for the first time (for example, you bought it new from a dealer)
      `the change takes it outside its RAV entry pathway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the modification would make the vehicle no longer meet the requirements of the entry pathway under which it was entered on the RAV
      `the rules allow the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Road Vehicle Standards Rules otherwise allow the modification
GIVETH A `May I modify it`
`May I modify this vehicle` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is on the Register of Approved Vehicles`)
    THEN `s 26 does not apply: the vehicle is not on the RAV`
    ELSE IF `it has already been provided to a consumer in Australia`
         THEN `the Act does not restrict it: s 26 applies only before the vehicle is first provided to a consumer in Australia; State or Territory law governs later modifications and use`
         ELSE IF (NOT `the change takes it outside its RAV entry pathway`)
              THEN `yes: the modification does not take it outside the entry pathway it was entered on the RAV under (s 26(1)(d))`
              ELSE IF `the rules allow the change`
                   THEN `yes: the rules allow the modification (s 26(1)(e))`
                   ELSE `no: the modification would contravene s 26, an offence and a civil penalty of up to 120 penalty units`

§§ `s 78 -- a new RAV vehicle on public roads, despite State or Territory standards`

-- s 78(1): "a road vehicle may be used in transport on a public road in a State or Territory, even though it does not comply
-- with a road vehicle standard imposed by a law of the State or Territory, if: (a) at the time the road vehicle is provided by
-- a person for the first time in Australia: (i) the vehicle is a new road vehicle; and (ii) the vehicle is on the RAV; and
-- (iii) the vehicle complies with the standards mentioned in subsection (3); and (b) the vehicle: (i) was manufactured or
-- provided by a constitutional corporation for use in transport; or (ii) is owned or used, or to be owned or used, by a
-- constitutional corporation; or (iii) is used ... predominantly in trade or commerce among the States or between a State
-- and a Territory; or (iv) is used, or to be used, in a Territory or Commonwealth place." (4): a State or Territory may still
-- prohibit or regulate its use if it ceases to comply with those standards or "the operation of the vehicle becomes
-- defective in any respect".
DECLARE `May I use it despite State standards` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it may be used on public roads even though it does not meet a State or Territory road vehicle standard (s 78(1))`
    `not under s 78: the State or Territory may prohibit or regulate its use, because it no longer complies with the national standards or has become defective (s 78(4))`
    `not under s 78: it was not a new vehicle on the RAV, complying with the national standards, when first provided in Australia (s 78(1)(a))`
    `not under s 78: none of the links to Commonwealth power in s 78(1)(b) applies`

@export Can my vehicle be used on public roads even though it does not meet a State or Territory vehicle standard?
GIVEN `it was new and on the RAV when first provided in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when first provided in Australia, the vehicle had not been used on a public road (other than to have work done, or to be protected, stored or transported) and was on the Register of Approved Vehicles
      `it then met the national standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it then complied with the national road vehicle standards that applied when it was entered on the RAV (or, if modified before then, the standards for it as modified)
      `a company made, supplied, owns or uses it, or it is used interstate or in a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a trading, financial or foreign corporation manufactured or provided it, or owns or uses it, or it is used mainly in trade or commerce between States, or it is used in a Territory or a Commonwealth place
      `it has stopped meeting those standards or become defective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has since ceased to comply with those national standards, or its operation has become defective in any respect
GIVETH A `May I use it despite State standards`
`Can my vehicle be used despite State standards` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`it was new and on the RAV when first provided in Australia` AND `it then met the national standards`))
    THEN `not under s 78: it was not a new vehicle on the RAV, complying with the national standards, when first provided in Australia (s 78(1)(a))`
    ELSE IF (NOT `a company made, supplied, owns or uses it, or it is used interstate or in a Territory`)
         THEN `not under s 78: none of the links to Commonwealth power in s 78(1)(b) applies`
         ELSE IF `it has stopped meeting those standards or become defective`
              THEN `not under s 78: the State or Territory may prohibit or regulate its use, because it no longer complies with the national standards or has become defective (s 78(4))`
              ELSE `yes: it may be used on public roads even though it does not meet a State or Territory road vehicle standard (s 78(1))`

§§ `Penalties -- ss 16-18, 22, 24, 26-32, 38-40, 56`

-- The maximum for an individual, in penalty units, as each provision states it; each is both an offence and a civil penalty
-- (the civil penalty figure is the same). s 29(4): "The maximum penalty for each day that an offence under subsection (2)
-- continues is 10% of the maximum penalty" (12 penalty units). ss 38(3), 39(2), 40(2): the figure for a person "not a body
-- corporate". A body corporate's figures (ss 35, 38-40) are not encoded: the seat is the individual.
DECLARE `What I did` IS ONE OF
    -- s 22
    `imported a road vehicle without being permitted to`
    -- s 24
    `provided a road vehicle for the first time in Australia when it was not on the RAV`
    -- s 16
    `entered a vehicle on the RAV that does not satisfy an entry pathway`
    -- s 17(1)
    `knowingly entered unauthorised or incorrect information on the RAV, or for a vehicle that does not exist`
    -- s 18
    `entered incorrect information on the RAV`
    -- s 26
    `modified a vehicle on the RAV, before it first reached a consumer, out of its entry pathway`
    -- s 27
    `falsely represented that a component I supplied was an approved road vehicle component`
    -- s 28
    `contravened a condition of an approval`
    -- s 29
    `did not export or destroy an imported vehicle within the period my import approval set`
    -- s 29(4)
    `each further day the vehicle is not exported or destroyed`
    -- s 30
    `did not keep a record, or give the Minister information, after my approval ended`
    -- s 31
    `knowingly signed a false or misleading declaration in an application for an approval`
    -- s 32
    `gave false or misleading information under the Act`
    -- s 38
    `did not comply with a recall notice, or supplied recalled vehicles or components`
    -- ss 39, 40
    `did not give the Minister a copy of a recall notice as the rules require`

@export What is the most I can be fined (in penalty units) for this contravention of the Road Vehicle Standards Act?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc What you did (or failed to do)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The most I can be fined in penalty units` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what I did`
    WHEN `entered incorrect information on the RAV` THEN 60
    WHEN `falsely represented that a component I supplied was an approved road vehicle component` THEN 60
    WHEN `did not keep a record, or give the Minister information, after my approval ended` THEN 60
    WHEN `knowingly signed a false or misleading declaration in an application for an approval` THEN 60
    WHEN `gave false or misleading information under the Act` THEN 60
    WHEN `each further day the vehicle is not exported or destroyed` THEN 12
    WHEN `did not comply with a recall notice, or supplied recalled vehicles or components` THEN 1050
    WHEN `did not give the Minister a copy of a recall notice as the rules require` THEN 16
    OTHERWISE 120

-- s 56(2) table: the infringement notice amount for a person "not a body corporate": 12 penalty units (s 38(3)), 6 penalty
-- units (s 39(2) or 40(2)), per alleged contravention, added together. For the Part 2 civil penalty provisions the amount
-- is the Regulatory Powers Act's (s 104(2)), not this Act's, and is not encoded (NOTHING).
@export If I am given an infringement notice for a recall contravention, what amount in penalty units will it state?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc What the infringement notice alleges
      `how many contraventions the notice alleges` IS A NUMBER @desc How many alleged contraventions of that kind the one notice deals with
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`The infringement notice amount in penalty units` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what I did`
    WHEN `did not comply with a recall notice, or supplied recalled vehicles or components` THEN JUST (12 TIMES `how many contraventions the notice alleges`)
    WHEN `did not give the Minister a copy of a recall notice as the rules require` THEN JUST (6 TIMES `how many contraventions the notice alleges`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

@export What is a number of penalty units in dollars?
GIVEN `the penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of penalty units
      `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of one penalty unit in dollars on the day of the offence (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, indexed)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The penalty units in dollars` MEANS `the penalty units` TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`
